-- title:
--   Tensor decomposition of S[[xsqcup y]]/(φ(x),φ(y))
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring, let $\sigma$ be a finite index set with decidable equality, let $\iota$ be a finite index set, and let $\varphi : \iota \to S[\![x_\sigma]\!]$ be a family of multivariate formal power series; write $I = \mathrm{span}(\mathrm{range}\,\varphi)$ for the ideal it generates. Assume there is a natural number $N$ such that for every $s \in \sigma$ the power $X_s^N$ lies in $I$. Consider the power series ring in the doubled variable set $\sigma \sqcup \sigma$ and the ideal $J$ generated by the union of the two families obtained from $\varphi$ by renaming the variables along $\mathrm{inl}$ and along $\mathrm{inr}$, i.e. by the $\varphi_i(x)$ together with the $\varphi_i(y)$. The assertion is that there exists an $S$-algebra isomorphism
--   $$e : S[\![x_\sigma \sqcup y_\sigma]\!]/J \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \bigl(S[\![x_\sigma]\!]/I\bigr) \otimes_S \bigl(S[\![x_\sigma]\!]/I\bigr)$$
--   which, on the classes of the split products, is given by $e\bigl(\overline{f(x)\,g(y)}\bigr) = \bar f \otimes \bar g$ for all $f, g \in S[\![x_\sigma]\!]$; here $f(x)$ and $g(y)$ denote the renamings of $f$ along $\mathrm{inl}$ and of $g$ along $\mathrm{inr}$, and the bars denote reduction modulo $I$.
--
--   This is the statement that, for an ideal containing a power of each variable, the quotient of a power series ring in two blocks of variables by the two renamed copies of the defining family is the ordinary (not completed) tensor product over $S$ of two copies of the one-block quotient — the algebraic counterpart of the product of two finite formal schemes. It is obtained from the base-change isomorphism [`MvPowerSeries.exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_quotient_span_map_of_pow_span_X_le`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.exists_algEquiv_tensorProduct_quotient_span_map_of_pow_span_X_le), and is used in [`MvPowerSeries.subst_sumElim_injective_of_finite_projective_quotient_of_X_pow_mem_span`](thm.html#MvPowerSeries.subst_sumElim_injective_of_finite_projective_quotient_of_X_pow_mem_span) to control substitution of two blocks of variables, as needed for comultiplications on finite formal group schemes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_algEquiv_quotient_sum_tensorProduct_quotient_apply_mk_rename_mul_rename.lean

